  "description": "Sundarban takes its name from the mangrove forest of the Bengal delta and gives children a small wooden play house with a single deck. A green slide comes off the deck, a climbing wall and a net climber lead up to it, and a nest swing hangs alongside. Children who prefer swinging to climbing still have something to do. Sundarban is compact, at 19'3\" x 12'3\", with a safe play area of 25'3\" x 18'3\". It takes 20 to 25 children and fits a preschool yard or the corner of a society garden. Skills listed are motor skills, self control and hand and eye coordination. It comes in mixed colours. We give a 3-year warranty on the galvanised pipe, roto-moulded slide, composite laminates and play rope. Share your corner size and we will check it.",
